1	# Item Detail Rebuild Implementation Plan
2	
3	> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
4	
5	**Goal:** Turn item detail from an edit form into what the design specifies — a read-first view that shows how you actually wear a piece, with editing moved behind the `⋯` overflow.
6	
7	**Architecture:** The screen inverts. `page.tsx` loads the item plus its wear history and a deterministic "goes with" set; the read view renders stats, tag rows and the complementary row; the existing form moves wholesale into a sheet opened from `⋯`. "Goes with" reuses the generator's own scoring — no new algorithm, no AI call.
8	
9	**Tech Stack:** Next.js 16 App Router, Supabase, Vitest, Motion.
10	
11	## Global Constraints
12	
13	- **Depends on two plans**: `2026-07-24-item-data-completeness.md` (price, colours, texture) and `2026-07-24-outfit-detail-wear-logging.md` (wear data). Three of the four stat tiles are empty without them.
14	- **TDD, strictly.** Branch: `feat/item-detail-rebuild`. No AI attribution.
15	- **No AI calls on this screen.** Everything here is a query or deterministic scoring.
16	- Test: `npx vitest run <path>` / `npm run test:run`. Types: `npx tsc --noEmit`. Build: `npm run build`.
17	
18	## Source
19	
20	`design_handoff_stylist_generator/Fitcheck.dc.html:587-657`. Review: `docs/design-review-2026-07-24.md` §1.
21	
22	## Decision required — read this before starting
23	
24	The design's primary CTA is **"Style an outfit with this"** (`:654`). That conflicts with Decision 5
25	(CLAUDE.md): looks are a daily drop, generated once per local day, and tapping an occasion reads stored
26	rows without calling the model. Styling around a chosen item is inherently on demand.
27	
28	**This plan assumes the cheap reading**, and Task 5 is written against it:
29	
30	> Tapping filters **today's already-stored looks** to those containing this item and opens the first
31	> match. If none contain it, the button offers *"Build a look around this"*, which runs a real
32	> generation and **consumes the regenerate quota** (`lib/outfits/quota.ts`).
33	
34	That keeps the free tier free, honours Decision 5, and gives the quota seam its first real consumer.
35	The alternative — an AI call on every tap — would make this button the largest per-user cost in the
36	product. **If you want that instead, change Task 5 before implementing it, not after.**
37	
38	Second assumption: **prices are GBP**, formatted with `Intl.NumberFormat("en-GB")`, because the design
39	prices Pro at `£5/mo` and shows `£3.28` cost-per-wear. A currency setting belongs to the Settings plan;
40	until it exists, one hard-coded currency beats a fake one.
